  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cash, Markets, Capacity Building and Evidence Generation In Support Of Vulnerable, Conflict-Affected Populations In Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cash Consortium of Sudan requests 5,000,000 GBP from FCDO to implement a harmonized and scaled approach to MPCA for basic needs. Mercy Corps leads the CCS, which includes Acted, CARE, IRC, NRC, and IMPACT. While Acted, CARE, IRC, and NRC are co-partners, IMPACT is the technical lead for assessment, monitoring, and evaluation. Ten Sudanese NGOs are also implementing partners and members of the CCS. The Action&#x2019;s outcome is to enable conflict-affected individuals to meet their basic needs, in particular by: 1.Providing Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance (MPCA) to vulnerable conflict-affected households to enable them to better meet their critical basic needs and reduce the use of negative coping strategies;2.Establishing a shock-responsive &#x2018;Common Fund&#x2019; crisis modifier to enable CCS partners to respond to onset shocks driven by conflict, climate, and/or epidemic outbreaks.The CCS is requesting for a top-up of 12,000,000 GBP to support CCS implementation from 1 April 2025 &#x2013; 31 March 2026. This contribution will build-on FCDO&#x2019;s funding of 9.5 million GBP, which supported implementation until March 2025. Through FCDO funding, the CCS, establishes an effective, efficient and people centred-response to the complex humanitarian emergency in Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
